  Method: every measurement is a passive capture of the DUT's own emissions, and every
  counted frame is matched on BOTH Ethernet MACs -- a poll is
  `[eth e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e]`, the DUT's SVI MAC to the supplicant's
  NIC MAC. Nothing rests on a supplicant COUNT; the deauthentication is attributed by
  the DUT's own log, which names the supplicant and its MAC. The negative legs
  (baseline, removal) are ZERO-frame rather than low-frame, and a count of zero cannot
  be inflated or masked by another station's traffic.

